Thought: The series has very strong seasonality and very unstable ranking; a simple robust mean may serve as a baseline and test the “robust” hint.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"mean","pool":"pool_full","rationale":"test robust baseline on highly seasonal, unstable ranking"}

Thought: The series has very high trend/seasonality but unstable ranking; try a weighted combo that favors low-error models but may overfit.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"inverse_error","rationale":"use inverse_error weighting to emphasize top models"}

Thought: The series has unstable ranking and many correlated errors; a softmax weighting may reduce overfitting compared to inverse_error.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"softmax_neg_error"}

Thought: Try a DBA strategy on the full pool to see if iterative refinement beats softmax.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"dba","pool":"pool_full","dba_max_iter":30,"rationale":"explore iterative weighted averaging"}

Thought: The series has strong seasonality but unstable ranking; a trimmed mean may reduce influence of outlier models.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"trimmed_mean","pool":"pool_full","trim_pct":0.2,"rationale":"trim extreme models in an unstable ranking"}

Thought: Ranking is unstable and many models are correlated; a forward‐selection weight may capture complementary strengths.  
Action: weights_forward  
Action Input: {"pool":"pool_full","max_steps":20,"metric":"rmse"}

Thought: test a robust non‑weighted average – median over the full pool, given strong seasonality and unstable ranking.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool_full","rationale":"median robust to outliers and ranking instability"}

Thought: test a forward‐selection weighted combo to see if it improves over median; forward selection may capture complementary models beyond top ones.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"w4","rationale":"forward selection weighting"}

Thought: Test a softmax_neg_error weighted combination to see if a smoother weighting improves over forward selection, given unstable ranking and high seasonality.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"softmax_neg_error","rationale":"softmax weighting may reduce overfitting in noisy, seasonal series"}

Thought: test per‑horizon weighting to handle unstable ranking and strong seasonality, using best_per_horizon which may adapt to horizon‑specific best models.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"best_per_horizon","rationale":"per‑horizon best model weighting to capture horizon‑dependent performance"}

Thought: Try a per‑horizon top‑k mean to capture horizon‑dependent strengths (seasonality high, ranking unstable).  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"weights_topk_per_horizon","k":3,"metric":"rmse"}

Thought: try a tighter trimmed mean to reduce influence of top outlier models given high outlier_pct and unstable ranking.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"trimmed_mean","trim_pct":0.1,"pool":"pool_full","rationale":"tighter trim to handle extreme errors"}

Thought: The series has very unstable ranking and many correlated errors; a per‑horizon top‑k mean might better capture horizon‑specific strengths than a global weight.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"weights_topk_per_horizon","k":5,"metric":"rmse"}

Thought: The series has unstable ranking and many correlated errors; a simple inverse‑error weighting may better balance the top models without over‑fitting.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: test a robust weighted scheme using softmax of negative error, which may handle unstable ranking and correlated errors better than inverse_error.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"softmax_neg_error"}

Thought: The series has very high trend/seasonality but ranking is unstable; selecting the top 5 models may reduce noise and then weighted by inverse_error could improve.  
Action: select_top_k  
Action Input: {"k":5,"metric":"rmse"}

Thought: The series has very high trend/seasonality but unstable ranking; a robust median over the top 5 models may perform well.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool4"}

Thought: The series has high trend/seasonality but ranking instability; a weighted combo on a smaller, more stable pool (pool4) with softmax weights may reduce overfitting.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool4","weights":"softmax_neg_error"}

